   "design": "Schema changes and queries start from drafts that must pass tests on a synthetic test copy, and the geneticist reviews every statement. A scripted import with validation rules loads submitted spreadsheets and rejects bad rows with reasons, instead of cleaning and pasting by hand; rules at import also prevent many later fixes. Backups run on a schedule, and accounts are created from requests approved in s6. The data dictionary is built from the schema and the geneticist adds explanations. Gathering needs, the data model, integrity checks, upgrades, access decisions and questions stay with the geneticist.",
